Explain waiting and bottlenecks through events, variation, and system boundaries (@mine-queues: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Reliability-availability-utilization-and-defined-denominators.lingua#r_0MV0F4CAPSWVG9GPC1S8PDS9RB") { r_7VKF3F1X78T6E5NJNV4SQYWBZX
**Read:** [A Review of Operations Research in Mine Planning — Newman and colleagues](../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS), the complete equipment/dispatch/simulation method selected and original paper; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the full capacity/handling context; [Reproducible computational work](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ), the complete relevant stochastic, validation, and performance studies.

Interacting equipment and work create queues, blocking, starvation, and changing bottlenecks. Mean cycle times or separate machine capacities can hide variability, synchronization, priorities, routes, failures, maintenance, and finite buffers. A larger fleet can increase waiting without increasing accepted output.

Little's relation L = λW connects long-run average population, throughput, and time in a consistently defined stable system under its conditions. For invented throughput 6 arrivals/departures h⁻¹ and mean system time 0.5 h, average population is 3. Define whether the system includes service or only waiting before comparing quantities.

A queue model must reflect the arrival/service/dependence and capacity assumptions appropriate to the question. An overloaded or changing system may not have the stationary average presumed by a simple formula. Discrete-event simulation needs event/state definitions, random-input evidence, warm-up/horizon, replications, and independent validation.

**Work:** derive/check the example and reconstruct a complete equipment/dispatch simulation study. Independently check conservation, deterministic limits, event timing, and measured performance not used for calibration. Compare a changed dispatch/maintenance or buffer policy with uncertainty and identify the actual controlling interface.

Read the complete relevant primary planning/dispatch paper and handbook capacity account. Shared reproducible/stochastic computing supports execution; the mine-specific model should preserve the work and material meaning behind its events.

